WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.240
- People quit all the time, 'cause

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:02.663
they're doing it for the money.

00:00:02.663 --> 00:00:03.740
(emotional piano music)

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.330
There's a debate, right now,
going on Twitter of like,

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:08.250
how many years do you
have to work until...

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.617
The hard work until the
thing, this guy's like,

00:00:10.617 --> 00:00:12.507
"Gary Vee, you said you
hustled your face off

00:00:12.507 --> 00:00:14.437
"for 10 years," he's
like, "I only had to do it

00:00:14.437 --> 00:00:16.520
"for two years, I couldn't
imagine doing it for 10."

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.447
And I'm laughing at him, and
another guy jumps in and goes,

00:00:19.447 --> 00:00:22.137
"Well, Gary said it best,
'Eat shit for blank years

00:00:22.137 --> 00:00:23.800
"and eat caviar for the
rest of your life.'"

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:27.060
Like, are you enjoying, is this fun?

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.827
I'm sure he's a lovely dude, is this fun?

00:00:29.827 --> 00:00:30.670
(they laugh)
That you're filming this?

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.480
Or are you doing it because you think

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.470
it's gonna get you to the
next level of success?

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:36.100
Do you love your process?

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.490
The gateway to happiness
is to love your process,

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:40.420
whatever that may be,
whether that creates wealth

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:43.980
or doesn't, if that creates
legacy and art or doesn't,

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:46.070
that creates impact on
the world or it doesn't.

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:48.890
You're clearly driven, like, you know,

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:49.920
first you wanted to be
in the NBA, (laughs)

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:54.920
then you wanted to be in the
PBA, then you wanted to act,

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.310
like, I think the thing that you need to

00:00:57.310 --> 00:00:59.690
understand is that you've got a gear

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:01.700
of motivation that makes you do.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:03.650
The first two things in
sports didn't work out,

00:01:03.650 --> 00:01:05.100
the thing that worked out in acting,

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.230
it did work out, whatever the definition

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:09.430
of what you're trying
to figure out right now,

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:11.410
it may or may not work.

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:14.170
What I'm excited about is the fact that

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:16.960
you've got a gear that
makes you want to do.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:18.840
I think one of the biggest
problems right now,

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.020
especially for people under
30 who want to be influencers

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:23.250
or entrepreneurs, which
is almost everybody,

00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.180
there's a lot of vanity metrics

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.327
that they're trying to
achieve to that mean nothing.

00:01:27.327 --> 00:01:29.300
"I raised 15 million dollars."

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.077
So? You might go out of business.

00:01:31.077 --> 00:01:32.810
"I've got a million subscribers."

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:33.643
So?

00:01:33.643 --> 00:01:35.080
"I've got 10 million subscribers."

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.860
So? I think, right now,

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:39.910
we live in a world that has so much data,

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:42.620
that people are living
towards the numbers.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:44.360
How many likes, how many followers,

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:45.950
how much capital I've raised.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:48.730
It's a, it becomes a numbers rack race,

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:50.940
and it usually leads to bad behavior,

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:52.890
because when you're chasing a number

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.780
that people can see, you
often take shortcuts.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:58.340
For me, the shit is the caviar.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.920
Like, I love the fuckin' process.

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:00.880
I love building.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.270
A very big reason acting
probably worked out was

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:05.560
you both thought it could bring you

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:06.530
something you were looking for

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:08.140
from the level of attention and success

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:11.240
and fame and dollars,
but you also liked it.

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:12.460
Because otherwise, if you didn't like it,

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:14.940
you would've quit after the
third "no" at auditions.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:17.170
When you do something for money, you quit.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:20.010
When you do it because you
love it, you do it forever.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.900
People win when they're self-aware.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.150
Some wanna make their bed, some don't.

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:28.090
Some have this strength,
some have that weakness.

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:30.378
You need to figure out who you are

00:02:30.378 --> 00:02:32.910
and you need to execute against that.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:35.650
You have to love the
process, not the stuff

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:37.670
that the process buys you.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:38.503
- [Woman In Audience] Yeah!

00:02:38.503 --> 00:02:40.370
(audience cheers)

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:41.490
- People quit all the time, 'cause

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:42.400
they're doing it for the money.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.467
I think the bigger question is,

00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:45.430
"what do you want the money for?"

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:48.854
Is it blocking an insecurity,
is it to get the girl,

00:02:48.854 --> 00:02:50.570
is it 'cause you're trying
to mass as much as you can

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.010
'cause you actually don't like
working and you wanna live--

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:56.280
The reason so many people
fail in life and business is,

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.827
their model is, "Let me get the money,

00:02:58.827 --> 00:03:01.470
"so then I can enjoy and relax."

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.000
They think of it as, like, hoarding it,

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.429
and then eating it all over
time, it's why retirement,

00:03:05.429 --> 00:03:08.000
(mumbles) it's such a bad
way to think about it,

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.670
because then you're feeling
the pressure of, like,

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:12.010
massing, so that you can then enjoy.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:13.080
I think the bigger question is, like,

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.660
what are you up to, why are
you doing it, what's up?

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:18.620
I just think a lot of people
are trying to achieve success

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:21.580
and use fame or money as makeup for

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:24.900
a situation that they're
just not happy about.

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.230
You have to figure out how to make

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:27.500
your day-in and day-out happy.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:28.970
It's all an inside game.

00:03:28.970 --> 00:03:31.770
You need to be enjoying
the amassing so much,

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:33.440
that you never get to the enjoying part.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:34.800
Otherwise, you're gonna be impatient,

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.620
and trying to be out of
it as quickly as possible,

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:38.960
to buy those things, or
you're gonna regret it

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.510
later in life, right?

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:43.190
I will never retire,
'cause it's not as fun

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:45.440
as working.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:46.810
Like, it's not as fun.

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:48.090
Like, it's very...

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:50.390
It's not as fun for me to lay on the beach

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:51.563
and play golf all day,

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:56.810
and lay on a yacht in the
middle of the Mediterranean

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:58.380
for a hundred days in the summer,

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:01.550
and go to vineyards and go
to concerts, and see friends,

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:02.940
that's not as fun

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:07.010
as fuckin' 15 hours of meetings all day.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:10.653
I don't wanna lay in a swan in a pool.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.010
I don't want to.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.010
That is what people have to figure out.

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:17.780
Whether that's singing, or being a mother,

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:20.800
or teaching a classroom,
to me, the game matters.

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:23.587
And by the way, somebody
may be looking, being like,

00:04:23.587 --> 00:04:27.957
"Gary, looks like shit, four
AM, six flights in Asia,

00:04:27.957 --> 00:04:29.440
"and I'm sitting here in Ibiza."

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:32.350
And for her or him, that's
winning, and that's great.

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:35.280
You've gotta try and figure that out

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.360
at all costs, and if
you're not happy right now,

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:40.310
you need to do something different.

00:04:40.310 --> 00:04:43.040
I just don't understand how...

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:46.850
People think wealth is
the gateway to happiness.

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.210
The gateway to happiness
is to love your process,

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:51.130
whatever that may be,
whether that creates wealth

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:54.810
or doesn't, if that creates
legacy and art or doesn't,

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.300
that creates impact on
the world or doesn't,

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:01.930
you've gotta try and figure
that out at all costs.

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:03.830
That if you're not happy right now,

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:05.770
you need to do something different.

00:05:05.770 --> 00:05:06.760
If you are not happy right now,

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:08.190
you have to break your patterns.

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:10.230
You have to look at life
from a different perspective.

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:12.993
You have to find a different
angle to look at it from.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:16.070
Because this shit goes
fast if you know it's long.

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:18.370
Figure out what your fucking winning is.

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:21.540
My winning is different
than a lot of people's.

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:24.820
I don't get envy, I get
excited, I get competitive,

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:26.920
I enjoy it, I enjoy my thing.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:29.830
What's your thing that
makes you the happiest...

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:31.240
- [Man] You just focus there.

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:32.273
- Only there.

00:05:33.278 --> 00:05:36.611
(emotional piano music)

